#: 76dd8b796dc64bc28589baecf87619a1
msgid "This article describes the mission commands that are supported by Copter, Plane, Sub and Rover when switched into Auto mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:8
#: 47881ee9c02849fcb6b788781e5a6826
msgid "there are many other MAVLink commands that a GCS or other device can send to the autopilot. See the ArduPilot/navlink repository, or the documentation for your GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:13
#: 7a44ba73da9540da85423a5cffada7ab
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:15
#: 917467e87eb7473ba72619d65de98063
msgid "The MAVLink protocol defines a large number of `MAV_CMD <https://github.com/ArduPilot/mavlink/blob/master/message_definitions/v1.0/common.xml#L1008>`__ waypoint command types (sent in a ``MAVLink_mission_item_message``). ArduPilot implements handling for the subset of these commands and command parameters that are *most relevant* and meaningful for each of the vehicles. Unsupported commands that are sent to a particular autopilot will simply be dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:23
#: 8e0669b039354ac5853145290c9512f2
msgid "This article lists and describes the commands and command-parameters that are supported on each of the vehicle types. Any parameter that is \"grey\" is not supported by the autopilot and will be ignored. They are still documented to make it clear which properties are supported by the `MAV_CMD protocol <https://github.com/ArduPilot/mavlink/blob/master/message_definitions/v1.0/common.xml#L1008>`__ are not implemented by the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:30
#: 99297f33270d42e9b1ed5e1d4ca3fee2
msgid "Some commands and command parameters are not implemented because they are not relevant for particular vehicle types (for example \"MAV_CMD_NAV_TAKEOFF\" command makes sense for Plane and Copter but not Rover and the pitch parameter only makes sense for Plane). There are also some potentially useful command parameters that are not handled because there is a limit to the message size, and a decision has been made to prioritize some parameters over others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:40
#: 93182f1bda5540f68fc936ee6cf25429
msgid "There is additional information about the supported commands on Copter (from a Mission Planner perspective) in the :ref:`Copter Mission Command List <copter:mission-command-list>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:44
#: bac8996f5efd4a919a29ff944d332193
msgid "Types of commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:46
#: 84bf930d51e1465eaded8dc2279b6b28
msgid "There are several different types of commands that can be used within missions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:49
#: d960ff9d987f409fbd1640cfcfb2ca5f
msgid "Navigation commands are used to control the movement of the vehicle, including takeoff, moving to and around waypoints, changing altitude, and landing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:52
#: 9bf923b0d9d1491984f7b955781d002c
msgid "DO commands are for auxiliary functions and do not affect the vehicle’s position (for example, setting the camera trigger distance, or setting a servo value)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:55
#: 9abdecc499524a5d8eab5a31a7efad29
msgid "Condition commands are used to delay DO commands until some condition is met, for example, the UAV reaches a certain altitude or distance from the waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:59
#: 01719934e7264b7ea6d2e28f8e07877b
msgid "During a mission at most one “Navigation” command and one “Do” or \"Condition\" command can be running at one time. A typical mission might set a waypoint (NAV command), add a CONDITION command that doesn't complete until a certain distance from the destination (:ref:`MAV_CMD_CONDITION_DISTANCE <mav_cmd_condition_distance>`), and then add a number of DO commands that are executed sequentially (for example :ref:`MAV_CMD_DO_SET_CAM_TRIGG_DIST <mav_cmd_do_set_cam_trigg_dist>` to take pictures at regular intervals) when the condition completes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:71
#: 8509c324b0ac43e0afc5f259925abfe8
msgid "CONDITION and DO commands are associated with the preceding NAV command: if the UAV reaches the next waypoint before these commands are executed, the next NAV command is loaded and they will be skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:80
#: 753fd3c8fbf64c9fbdafbb689279440a
msgid "Frames of reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:82
#: 0f61b1f44fdf4c0e951e6d219cd1022a
msgid "Many of the commands (in particular the :ref:`NAV\\_ commands <common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd_navigation_commands>`) include position/location information. The information is provided relative to a particular \"frame of reference\", which is specified in the message's :ref:`common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd_navigation_commands_frames` field. Copter and Rover Mission use :ref:`MAV_CMD_DO_SET_HOME <mav_cmd_do_set_home>` command to set the \"home position\" in the global coordinate frame (MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL), `WGS84 coordinate system <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Geodetic_System>`__, where the altitude is relative to mean sea level. All other commands use the MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT frame, which uses the same latitude and longitude, but sets altitude as relative to the *home position* (home altitude = 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:92
#: 273ca92353dd4e678879ff0950aab868
msgid "Plane commands can additionally use MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_TERRAIN_ALT frame of reference. This again has the same WGS84 frame of reference for latitude/longitude, but specifies altitude relative to ground height (as defined in a terrain database)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:99
#: cd8b7992f5ca4c5488834fed045da913
msgid "The other frame types are defined in the MAVLink protocol (see `MAV_FRAME <https://github.com/ArduPilot/mavlink/blob/master/message_definitions/v1.0/common.xml#L795>`__) are not supported for mission commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:104
#: 1011c801d4294b46af9aa1f99124bd52
msgid "How accurate is the information?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:106
#: 99644d91c6df408bb3b948e5aeb31079
msgid "If a command or parameter is marked as supported then it is likely (but not guaranteed) that it will behave as indicated. If a command or parameter is not listed (or marked as not supported) then it is extremely likely that it is not supported on ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:111
#: 212b5afd2cfd4a5599b6daf34ab0785a
msgid "The reason for this is that the information was predominantly inferred by inspecting the command handlers for messages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:114
#: 080db69ed2674ad7b174afb0808ef357
msgid "The switch statement in `AP_Mission::mavlink_to_mission_cmd <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Mission/AP_Mission.cpp#L466>`__ was inspected to determine which commands are handled by *all* vehicle platforms, and which parameters from the message are stored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:117
#: 4bb231039aa24d089313e5c657bf7a23
msgid "The command handler switch for each vehicle type (`Plane <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduPlane/commands_logic.cpp#L33>`__, `Copter <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/commands_logic.cpp#L49>`__, `Rover <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Rover/commands_logic.cpp#L25>`__) tells us which commands are likely to be supported in each vehicle and which parameters are passed to the handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:124
#: 1d01b3081e2d4b8a85cfe093c17c160e
msgid "The above checks give a very accurate picture of what commands and parameters are not supported. They give a fairly accurate picture of what commands/parameters are *likely to be supported*. However, this indication is not guaranteed to be accurate because a command handler could just throw away all the information (and we have not fully checked all of these)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd.rst:131
#: b78d879671da474eb770f19e49c42e8e
msgid "In addition to the above checks, we have also merged information from the :ref:`Copter Mission Command List <copter:mission-command-list>`."
msgstr ""

